{"@type":"Question","name":"What's the minimum order for a t-shirt style?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"300 pieces per style for OEM and ODM orders, split across sizes and up to 3 colors within that style. Blank CMT (cut-make-trim) orders where you supply the fabric run at a 5,000-piece minimum, since fabric sourcing and dyeing lots don't scale efficiently below that."}},
{"@type":"Question","name":"What GSM should I choose for my t-shirt line?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"It depends on positioning and climate. 140-160gsm suits hot-climate retail and fashion-forward drapey fits; 180-200gsm is the safest default for general retail; 200-220gsm suits streetwear brands wanting a boxier, more structured feel. We can send physical swatches at multiple weights before you commit."}},
{"@type":"Question","name":"Can you produce private label t-shirts with my own brand tags?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. Private label is our default setup for most t-shirt clients — your neck labels, hang tags, and packaging, our production. We handle woven label sourcing and can work from your existing label supplier if you already have one."}},
{"@type":"Question","name":"What printing and decoration methods do you offer for t-shirts?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Screen printing and embroidery are done in-house. DTF and sublimation for all-over prints are handled through vetted partner facilities we manage directly, so you still deal with one point of contact and one quality sign-off. Screen printing is the most cost-effective option above roughly 100 pieces per design; DTF suits smaller runs or designs with many colors and gradients."}},
